<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02GH">Construction <span data-tag="02GH">4.6.4.15</span> <span class="named">(The Slice Diagonal Morphism)</span>.</a> Let $F: K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets, and let $c: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \diamond K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \star K$ be the comparison morphism of Notation <a data-tag="01HR" href="/tag/01HR">4.6.2.3</a>. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="01KN" href="/tag/01KN">4.6.4.11</a>, the composite map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \diamond K \xrightarrow {c} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \star K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> determines a morphism of simplicial sets $\delta _{/F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/F} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\vec{\times }_{ \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \{ F\} $, which we will refer to as the <em>slice diagonal morphism</em>. Similarly, the composition </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  K \diamond \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} \rightarrow K \star \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}} \]
</div>
<p> determines a morphism of simplicial sets $\delta _{F/}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{F/} \rightarrow \{ F\}  \vec{\times }_{ \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, which we will refer to as the <em>coslice diagonal morphism</em>. </p>
</article>
